# Secrets never get committed. The cloud job writes .env from GitHub secrets at
# run time and deletes it before committing; locally it holds your real keys.
.env

# Raw answer transcripts (about 700 small text files per run) are committed so
# the cockpit's "view answer" works for cloud runs, not just local ones. They
# also still ship as a downloadable workflow artifact as a backup. If the repo
# ever feels heavy from these, revisit moving them to object storage (R2/S3).

# Scratch and build noise.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.bak
*.log
